 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t an objective “best” lawyer for every truck accident case. If I had to suggest one Dallas attorney to start with, **Quentin Brogdon** is worth considering: he is listed as board-certified in Personal Injury Trial Law and focuses on commercial truck accidents. Board certification is a useful credential, but it doesn’t guarantee a particular result.\n\nI’d compare him with at least two other truck-accident attorneys and ask:\n- Who will personally handle the case?\n- How many commercial-truck cases have they taken to trial?\n- How will they preserve evidence such as driver logs, electronic data, and maintenance records?\n- What are the contingency fee and case expenses?\n\nConfirm credentials and disciplinary history with the State Bar of Texas, and don’t sign until you understand the fee agreement.",
